A||||2||KevinR||Fuel Gauge stuck on full||||5||
Z||000000||KevinR||06-11-2001||12:56 PM||||HELP! is there an easy fix for this? It doesnt appear that the needle is hung up at all but it is pegged all the to full.||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||06-11-2001||06:44 PM||||Hope this helps.  Not exactly easy.  At work I would have to access back of I/P cluster and check resistance of fuel level sensor.<BR>90 ohms at full<BR>0 ohms empty<P>terminal is c3-7 is a pink wire||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||06-12-2001||04:50 AM||||Recently I had to drop my gas tank to fix my pegging gas gauge. All the connections on the sending unit were gummed up.  I took the sending unit completely apart, sanded and cleaned all the connections.  Now it works just find.  My symptoms were intermittent pegging past full.  Apparently when the sending unit doesn't make a connection, your gauge will peg.  If I were your I would first disconnect the sending unit wire harness in the engine compartment (below the batter to the left) then put a 0 ohm/ 90 ohm resistance.  It should read full and empty as you change the resistance.<P>You can also try and dump a can of gas cleaner in your tank to unclog things.  It did help my problem, but did not solve it completely||||reg||1
